// EXPECT: [E086]
// EXPECT-TEXT: unsigned left shift may lose bits
// `x << 63` keeps only x's lowest bit: for any x past 1 a bit is lost, which a checked `<<` owes not to
// happen. The judge's record there is a `narrow` one (the result fits u64), and the message says so.
// It read "shift amount is not provably within the operand's width", VRA's words for a different
// check at the same instruction, though 63 is within a u64's width (TCW, 2026-10-26).
func top(x u64) u64 {
    return x << 63
}
func main() i32 {
    var a u64 = top(1)
    return 0
}
